    "['unit [parameter2] tunnel destination [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface Tunnel1', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface Tunnel1\\n tunnel destination 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, you would typically also need to configure the tunnel source separately (equivalent to Juniper's `set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 1 tunnel source 10.1.1.1`), and the tunnel interface numbering is arbitrary (I used Tunnel1 as an example). The complete tunnel configuration would require additional parameters in Cisco to match the Juniper 6RD functionality.\", 'trans_template': 'interface Tunnel1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel destination 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface Tunnel1\\n tunnel destination 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, you would typically also need to configure the tunnel source separately (equivalent to Juniper's `set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 1 tunnel source 10.1.1.1`), and the tunnel interface numbering is arbitrary (I used Tunnel1 as an example). The complete tunnel configuration would require additional parameters in Cisco to match the Juniper 6RD functionality.\", 'trans_template': 'tunnel destination 0.0.0.0'}]]": 1,
