    "['set services 6rd ipv4-prefix-length [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 6rd prefix 2001:db8::/32 8', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ipv6 6rd prefix 2001:db8::/32 8', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nipv6 6rd prefix 2001:db8::/32 8\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command `set services 6rd ipv4-prefix-length 8` sets the IPv4 prefix length for 6rd (IPv6 Rapid Deployment) tunneling to 8 bits.\\n- The equivalent Cisco command combines both the IPv6 prefix and IPv4 prefix length into a single command.\\n- The Cisco format is: `ipv6 6rd prefix <ipv6-prefix> <ipv4-prefix-length>`\\n- We include the IPv6 prefix (2001:db8::/32) from the Juniper configuration since it's required for the Cisco command to be complete.\", 'trans_template': 'ipv6 6rd prefix 2001:db8::/32 8'}]]": 1,
